WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.567
The Ukrainian

00:00:00.567 --> 00:00:00.967
capital of

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.002
Kiev is bracing

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.770
for more drone strikes tonight

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.972
after the Kremlin blamed Ukraine

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.907
for a drone attack on Moscow,

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.409
the first to hit civilian areas.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:10.977
And the Russian capital.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.379
Several residential buildings

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:14.581
were damaged and two people were injured.

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:15.582
Ukraine denies

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:17.617
any direct involvement in this attack,

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.152
but it's the latest sign

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.487
that the war could be entering

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.721
a new phase.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.223
President Vladimir Zelensky

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:23.990
has even said

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.892
the timing of Ukraine's counteroffensive

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.227
has been set.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:29.429
CNN's Jim Sciutto is here to break down

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.130
the very latest.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.164
A lot has been going on

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.732
these last 24 hours.

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.000
You bring us up to speed.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.301
So biggest thing is

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.237
that Ukraine is proving its ability

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.638
to strike in Russian

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.572
controlled territory.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.775
Russian controlled territory inside

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.576
Ukraine taken over since the invasion,

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:44.411
but also

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.047
crucially inside Russia here, Kursk,

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.782
across the border in Belgorod,

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.850
Vantage.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:51.918
But in Moscow

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.521
and on civilian targets there,

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.189
it seems with drones.

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:56.856
Now, Ukraine

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.491
has not claimed responsibility,

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.693
but they have not denied

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.595
direct responsibility for this.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.064
But the key seems to be

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.765
showing it ability to attack

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:07.801
behind enemy lines,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.669
even on the Russian homeland.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.671
And the crucial timing here

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:12.105
is that

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:14.274
in advance of this highly anticipated

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.975
Ukrainian counteroffensive,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.111
showing an ability to attack there,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.513
but also keeping Russia on its toes,

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.481
so to speak.

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.382
You know,
they don't know

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.683
where they might strike next.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.084
Yeah.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.119
I mean, it seems as though it is.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:26.553
I mean,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.021
Vladimir Putin, for his part, has said

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.756
this is terrorist activity.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.124
As you point out, though,

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.592
Ukrainians, top officials,

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.493
they are saying

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.395
we did not have direct

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.729
keyword involvement

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.031
in what happened in Moscow.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:38.731
What more do we know

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.233
about how these drones were used

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.101
and who could be behind them?

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.303
So we don't know what specific

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.070
drones were used.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.505
We do know that in the past,

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.340
Ukraine has

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.843
used old Soviet era drones.

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.078
Listen, this goes back to the seventies,

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:54.114
not as capable of drones as drones

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.548
as we know today.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.783
But to your point,

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.718
they don't deny

00:01:58.718 --> 00:01:59.519
directly

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.053
that were there

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:02.055
denying direct, direct responsibility.

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:02.922
They're not denying

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.124
any responsibility here.

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.291
And that's key because,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.392
listen, we've talked a lot

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.494
about the Ukraine war.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.294
Russia throughout

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.696
the war has attacked

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.097
Ukrainian civilian sites

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.065
in Kiev repeatedly,

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.101
including horribly in the last 24 hours

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.402
and going back

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.004
all across the country here.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.405
So for Ukraine

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.006
to attack

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.541
a civilian target inside

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:25.411
Russia is a step and could create tension

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.781
between Ukraine and its NATO's backers

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.183
and the U.S.

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.218
for attacking civilian targets

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.153
because it has given them

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.787
the moral high ground

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.756
not to attack civilian targets.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.291
To this point. Right.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.592
And of course,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.127
allies, including the US,

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.696
have given Ukraine tons of weapons.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.698
But there's always been that concern

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.699
or that precondition

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:47.734
this should not be used.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.102
That could be the red line here.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.171
It's not clear that Ukraine has used

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:51.804
in fact,

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.039
there's no evidence that Ukraine

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:55.141
has used Western supplied weapons to

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.177
to strike Russian territory,

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.412
certainly civilian targets in Moscow,

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.281
and that could create divisions

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.049
between Ukraine

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:04.717
and its Western backers

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.953
if it were to use such weapons to do so.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:07.587
Given

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.822
all the and purely understandable

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.725
and justifiable anger that the U.S.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:15.495
and Western allies have have expressed

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.663
due to Russia's attack,

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:17.430
Russia's attacks

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.632
on civilian targets inside Ukraine.

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:20.967
Yeah, but it's interesting, too,

00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:22.168
that the US supplied

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.770
Patriot missiles have really been helping

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.804
save lives there

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.339
in Ukraine in the wake of those attacks.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:26.906
No question.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.775
And they've been very successful.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.410
And we should not

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.711
equate the two of these things

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.179
because Russia has been attacking,

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:33.713
first of all.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.347
Russia attacked

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.949
Ukraine unprovoked

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:36.883
and it's been tried

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.084
in civilian targets for

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.852
for close to a year and a half

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.588
since since it invaded Ukraine

00:03:41.588 --> 00:03:42.522
going back to February.

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:43.690
Can't lose sight of that for sure.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.858
Jim Sciutto, thank you so much.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:46.893
Well, let's get more perspective

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:47.827
now from former U.S.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.562
ambassador to NATO, Kurt Volker.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.631
He was also the US special envoy

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.165
to Ukraine.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:52.999
Ambassador Volker,

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:53.967
thanks for coming on tonight

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.001
to this morning.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.169
Russian President Putin

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.238
responded to the Moscow drone attacks.

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.372
Here's what he said.

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:03.710
He's here.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.877
Do you know

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.080
Kiev chose the path of intimidation

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.781
of Russian citizens and attacks

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.516
on residential buildings.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.885
It is a clear sign of terrorist activity.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.456
So calling this terrorist

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.457
activity suggests

00:04:17.457 --> 00:04:18.958
how seriously he takes this

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.860
and the kind of response he could take.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.362
Do you think Putin might use

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.696
this moment as grounds

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.999
for even more severe tactics

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:28.768
Well, first off,

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.436
I think if Putin could use

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.638
more severe tactics,

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.706
he would already be doing it.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:35.241
His forces are doing very badly

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.142
in Ukraine.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:37.644
He's escalated the attacks

00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:39.646
on Ukrainian cities already.

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:41.281
If he could do more, he would.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.982
And I think his messaging here

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:45.318
is really about trying to reassure

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.653
the Russian public

00:04:46.653 --> 00:04:48.688
who have got to be freaking out

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.123
that there are actually attacks

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.958
happening inside Russia now,

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:54.160
something that they had not seen before.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:54.861
He's called this

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:56.896
a special military operation.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:58.965
He has said that this is,

00:04:58.965 --> 00:04:59.332
you know,

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:01.367
responding against

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.468
NATO's responding

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.237
against Nazis in Ukraine.

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:05.505
And now all of a sudden, there's

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:06.272
actually something

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:07.840
happening inside Russia.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.242
This is putting pressure on him

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:11.611
and he's trying to control the narrative.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.313
What does that do

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:16.049
in terms of public sentiment in Russia?

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:18.151
The fact that Russian civilians

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:19.986
are now feeling the effects

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.854
of this war on their own soil

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:24.524
Well, the first thing

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.025
is I think it's bringing home to them

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:28.328
the idea that this is actually a war.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:30.063
Putin has tried to portray

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:32.432
this as a special military operation

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:33.933
far away,

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.069
dealing with something inside Ukraine

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.670
and fully justified.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.172
And the fact that this is not

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:39.906
what's happening

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.841
is already evident to lots of people.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.776
Russia's lost so many people,

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:44.777
so much equipment.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.546
The war has gone on so long.

00:05:46.546 --> 00:05:47.513
And now that they see

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.614
something inside Russia,

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:51.150
I think it adds to that confusion.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:52.585
But one thing I want to come back to what

00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:53.386
Jim Sciutto said,

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.154
which is making an assumption

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.622
that Ukraine was targeting

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.224
civilian targets.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.659
We don't know that.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:00.993
We don't know what the targets were

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:01.361
because

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:03.463
all of the drones that were fired

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:05.198
were shot down by Russia.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.866
We don't know where they were going.

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:08.601
It could have been military targets.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:09.602
We don't know.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.637
We also don't know where they were fired

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.172
from. Or who did it.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.208
And so I think we all have to assume

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:16.142
that Ukraine

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:18.211
would have facilitated this in some way.

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:19.712
But there's a lot we don't know.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.714
So we shouldn't jump to assumptions.

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:22.982
Let's talk more about that.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.984
And as Jim emphasized, you know,

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:26.686
Ukraine is

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:29.889
basically denying direct involvement.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:32.024
But how critical credible is that?

00:06:32.058 --> 00:06:32.525
I mean,

00:06:32.525 --> 00:06:34.460
clearly, very careful words

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.461
selection there.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:36.396
How credible is it,

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:37.597
especially given our previous

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:38.331
reporting that U.S.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.399
intelligence picked up

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:41.234
chatter of Ukrainian officials blaming

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.002
each other for the Kremlin drone attack?

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.438
Yeah, well,

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:46.005
the first thing

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.206
is that remember last week

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:48.241
we saw these attacks

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:50.576
inside Russian territory in Belgorod

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.979
And these were all Russians

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.014
who are against Vladimir Putin

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.949
and who gathered some military equipment,

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:58.017
made an incursion

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:59.719
just to prove a point that they could do.

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.488
So they probably could not have done that

00:07:02.688 --> 00:07:04.056
without some kind of tacit

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.491
Ukrainian support.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:06.392
But at the same time,

00:07:06.392 --> 00:07:08.361
it wasn't Ukrainians doing it

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:10.696
wasn't Ukraine conducting the attacks

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:12.899
as far as the drones go.

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:14.534
We don't know where they're fired from.

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.035
And I think that's significant

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:17.670
because it's a long way

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.739
from the Ukrainian border to Moscow

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:22.041
with a lot of air defenses along the way.

00:07:22.442 --> 00:07:23.342
So for these drones

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:24.877
to get there, it indicates to me

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:27.046
they probably weren't fired from Ukraine.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.415
But somewhere inside Russia,

00:07:29.415 --> 00:07:31.117
even then, we don't know who did it.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:33.186
It could be Ukrainian special forces.

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:33.886
It could be

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.755
these kind of Russian partizans,

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:37.590
and it could be facilitated by Ukraine

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.291
in some way.

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:39.292
There's just a lot

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:41.527
that is unclear about all of this.

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:42.562
All right, Kurt Volker,

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:43.529
thank you for offering your

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:44.497
perspective tonight.

